Chapter: GopShot
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopRtc

 The screen, written to the boot stick as a BMP -- the telemetry channel
 that retires the camera: a photograph names what a reader can decode
 from it, a pixel-exact frame names everything. One keystroke on the
 desktop captures the live framebuffer and lands SHhhmmss.BMP on the
 stick's own ESP, named by the RTC so no directory scan is needed and
 two shots collide only within one second.

 We say:

Section: BMP Encoding

 BITMAPFILEHEADER (14 bytes) then BITMAPINFOHEADER (40): magic "BM",
 file size, pixel offset 54; header size 40, width, height POSITIVE for
 bottom-up rows, one plane, 24 bits per pixel, no compression, image
 size, 2835 pixels-per-metre both axes. Rows pad to four bytes. The
 framebuffer's 32-bit pixels are B,G,R,X in memory order and BMP wants
 B,G,R, so the copy takes the low three bytes of each pixel as they lie.

  shot-row-bytes : Integer -> Integer
  shot-row-bytes (w) = bit-and (w * 3 + 3) (-4)

  shot-header : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shot-header (buf) (w) (h) (size) =
    let a = poke-byte buf 0 66
    in let b = poke-byte buf 1 77
    in let c = gfat-put-u32 buf 2 size
    in let d = gfat-put-u32 buf 6 0
    in let e = gfat-put-u32 buf 10 54
    in let f = gfat-put-u32 buf 14 40
    in let g = gfat-put-u32 buf 18 w
    in let i = gfat-put-u32 buf 22 h
    in let j = gfat-put-u16 buf 26 1
    in let k = gfat-put-u16 buf 28 24
    in let l = gfat-put-u32 buf 30 0
    in let m = gfat-put-u32 buf 34 (size - 54)
    in let n = gfat-put-u32 buf 38 2835
    in let o = gfat-put-u32 buf 42 2835
    in let p = gfat-put-u32 buf 46 0
    in gfat-put-u32 buf 50 0

  shot-copy-row : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shot-copy-row (dst) (src) (w) (x) =
    if x >= w then 0
    else let a = poke-byte dst (x * 3) (peek-byte src (x * 4))
    in let b = poke-byte dst (x * 3 + 1) (peek-byte src (x * 4 + 1))
    in let c = poke-byte dst (x * 3 + 2) (peek-byte src (x * 4 + 2))
    in shot-copy-row dst src w (x + 1)

  shot-copy-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shot-copy-rows (buf) (base) (w) (h) (stride) (rb) (y) =
    if y >= h then 0
    else let r = shot-copy-row (buf + 54 + y * rb) (base + (h - 1 - y) * stride * 4) w 0
    in shot-copy-rows buf base w h stride rb (y + 1)

Section: Naming

 An 8.3 directory name is eleven ASCII bytes, space-padded, no dot:
 "SHhhmmssBMP". The bytes are poked as ASCII directly -- Text here is
 CCE and a CCE byte on a FAT directory entry is a name no other reader
 resolves.

  shot-digit2 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shot-digit2 (buf) (off) (v) =
    let a = poke-byte buf off (48 + v / 10)
    in poke-byte buf (off + 1) (48 + int-mod v 10)

  shot-name : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shot-name (buf) (hh) (mm) (ss) =
    let a = poke-byte buf 0 83
    in let b = poke-byte buf 1 72
    in let c = shot-digit2 buf 2 hh
    in let d = shot-digit2 buf 4 mm
    in let e = shot-digit2 buf 6 ss
    in let f = poke-byte buf 8 66
    in let g = poke-byte buf 9 77
    in poke-byte buf 10 80

  shot-bcd : Integer -> Integer
  shot-bcd (n) = (n / 16) * 10 + int-mod n 16

  shot-pad2 : Integer -> Text
  shot-pad2 (n) = if n < 10 then "0" & show n else show n

Section: Capture

 The caller brackets this with __heap-save / __heap-restore AFTER using
 the returned Text: the frame buffer copy and the FAT image both live on
 the heap and a desktop that leaks megabytes per keystroke halts in
 minutes. The answer Text names the file on success and the failing
 stage otherwise, ready to paint.

  shot-take : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Text
  shot-take (base) (w) (h) (stride) = act
    m <- gfat-mount-esp
    if m.gm-ok == False then "shot: no ESP mount"
    else act
      rh <- rtc-read 4
      rm <- rtc-read 2
      ss <- rtc-seconds 0
      let hh = shot-bcd rh
      in let mi = shot-bcd rm
      in let s2 = if ss < 0 then 0 else ss
      in let rb = shot-row-bytes w
      in let size = 54 + rb * h
      in let buf = alloc-zeroed (bit-and (size + 511) (-512)) 64
      in let hd = shot-header buf w h size
      in let px = shot-copy-rows buf base w h stride rb 0
      in let nb = alloc-zeroed 16 16
      in let nm = shot-name nb hh mi s2
      in act
        ok <- gfat-write-file (m.gm-vol) nb buf size
        if ok then "shot SH" & shot-pad2 hh & shot-pad2 mi & shot-pad2 s2 & ".BMP ok" else "shot write FAILED"
      end
    end
  end
